00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:35.180
Imagine you bought an ETF tracking the TSX last week after it bounced from the 50-day moving

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:42.100
average. Your order filled at the ask, but the real mechanics involved the bid ask spread widening

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:48.360
from three cents to 12 cents in the first 20 minutes of the session, because volume was only 60%

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:54.000
of the 20-day average. Support and resistance are simply price levels where buying or selling

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:59.820
pressure historically clustered. The 200-day moving average often acts as dynamic support in

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:07.040
uptrends while the 50-day serves as a shorter-term trend filter. RSI measures momentum on a 0-100

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:13.040
scale, with readings below 30 flagging oversold conditions that have preceded rebounds in roughly

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:20.900
65% of cases over the past decade on large cap indices. MACD tracks the convergence or divergence

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:27.200
of two exponential moving averages and generates crossovers that work best as confirmation rather

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:33.720
than standalone signals. Volume analysis adds conviction because a breakout above resistance on

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:40.020
volume 150% above average has shown higher follow-through rates than low volume moves.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:45.200
The biggest mistake with technical analysis is treating it as a directional predictor

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:51.680
instead of an entry and exit timing tool. Instead, always combine at least two indicators with a

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:57.700
fundamental catalyst before committing capital. Open your brokerage platform, pull up alphabet

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:04.740
